{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwistedChannelSplitting"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_monotone_deuteron_binds_less","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_monotone_deuteron_binds_less","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L175-L181","doc":"Cell (negative twist, monotone `B`): the deuteron binds **less** than the singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_monotone_deuteron_binds_more","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_monotone_deuteron_binds_more","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L167-L173","doc":"Cell (positive twist, monotone `B`): the deuteron binds **more** than the singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_antitone_deuteron_binds_more","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_antitone_deuteron_binds_more","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L159-L165","doc":"Cell (negative twist, antitone `B`): the deuteron binds **more** than the singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_antitone_deuteron_binds_less","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_antitone_deuteron_binds_less","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L151-L157","doc":"Cell (positive twist, antitone `B`): the deuteron binds **less** than the singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.binds_more_of_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.binds_more_of_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L144-L147","doc":"Monotone binding: the larger trace binds more. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.binds_less_of_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.binds_less_of_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L137-L141","doc":"Antitone binding (the direction of every working form in the corpus): the larger trace binds\nless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_twist_D_lt_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.negative_twist_D_lt_S","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L117-L124","doc":"**Negative orientation.**  A spin-only twist acting by `θ_λ^{−k}` makes the deuteron channel\ntrace the smaller: `D < S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_twist_D_gt_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.positive_twist_D_gt_S","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L108-L115","doc":"**Positive orientation.**  A spin-only twist acting by `θ_λ^k` (`k ≥ 1`) makes the deuteron\nchannel trace the larger: `S < D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_inv_pow_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_inv_pow_lt","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L90-L100","doc":"For `q > 1`, the inverse (negative-orientation) twist reverses the order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_pow_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_pow_lt","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L78-L88","doc":"For `q > 1`, the ribbon eigenvalue on `(4,2)` exceeds that on `(3,3)`, and so does every\npositive power `k` of it (`k = 1` ribbon, `k = 2` full twist). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_three_three_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.theta_three_three_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L74-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.split_neg_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.split_neg_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L62-L68","doc":"If the twist's eigenvalue on the deuteron's spin block is the smaller one, then `D < S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.split_pos_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwistSplitSignDictionary.split_pos_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwistSplitSignDictionary.lean#L53-L60","doc":"If the twist's eigenvalue on the deuteron's spin block exceeds that on the singlet's, and the\nblock traces have positive product, then `D > S`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}